        <briefdescription>
<para>constructs a node manifold accessing the supplied node colony and node pointers </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Creates a node manifold from the 2 pointers to co-located nodes. Additional nodes can be added to it later.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nodes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>reference to the primary storage of the nodes in the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_mesh_manager" kindref="compound">MeshManager</ref> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>inside</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>pointer to the node that will assumed to be on the INSIDE of the interface that that manifold is part of </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>outside</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>opposing yet collocated node in the manifold </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>manifold_type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>geometric classifier of the new manifold, default is INTERFACE but may need to be revised if the node is at a model boudary or other. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>an iterator to the new manifold stored in a colony in the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_node_manifold_manager" kindref="compound">NodeManifoldManager</ref>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>this method does not assign the nodes to the new manifold.; this must be done by calling Node::Assign( manifold ) after its successful creation which only happens on the return from this method. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
